source: crates/daemon/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Measure drafting with your LLM. Nothing is saved or sent.

With --set mine (the default), replay your most recent replies: draft each one from what was known just before you replied and compare it with what you sent (greeting, sign-off, length, invented numbers). With --set quick, draft each labelled compose case and grade it against what that case required (kept sentences, answers, gaps, invented numbers, length, leftovers). Calls your drafting LLM once per case. --rewrite also runs the configured humanizer rewrite model for each replay. Uses --account with --set mine.

Usage: mxr draft eval [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --limit <LIMIT>
          How many replies to replay, at most 50 (--set mine only)

          [default: 10]

      --set <SET>
          Which cases to draft

          Possible values:
          - mine:  Your most recent replies, replayed
          - quick: The labelled compose corpus, graded check by check

          [default: mine]

      --rewrite
          Also run the configured humanizer rewrite model for each replay

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
